1
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,320
Thank you.

2
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,577
There's nothing else in the world
It's so much love I don't want to lose

3
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:09,477
my dreams I don't want to lose my life

4
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,600
All my life

5
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:36,937
After reaching the continent of Server,

6
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:40,726
we found a Koromon village, but
it was occupied by the Pagumon.

7
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:44,080
Later, during dinner, Poyomon
digivolved to Tokomon.

8
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:47,439
That night, little Toko was
taken from our campsite.

9
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:50,737
Agumon finally found him and
all the Koromon in a cave.

10
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:52,797
They were being guarded by the Gazimon,

11
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,177
who were also planning on
giving us to their leader,

12
00:01:55,260 --> 00:01:57,557
that rock and roll digi-jerk Etemon.

13
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:01,217
He used his music like a weapon
and tried to destroy the village.

14
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,997
We found the crest for Ty's tag,
and it created an escape for us.

15
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:06,280
Never a dull moment.

16
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:18,360
Oh, how far do we have to walk?

17
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,216
Until Etemon can't follow us anymore.

18
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,578
I don't think there is such a place.

19
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,437
We certainly can't stop here
in the middle of nowhere.

20
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:30,814
For one thing, if we were attacked,
there'd be no place for us to run to.

21
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:33,166
This is starting to look bad.

22
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:35,813
Everyone's becoming so timid and afraid.

23
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:37,800
Hey, come on, you guys.

24
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:38,980
Why'd we stop?

25
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,591
Why's everyone so scared?

26
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,897
After all, we do have the crest, you know.

27
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:46,697
That's true, but do we really know the
crest will help Agumon to Digivolve?

28
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,610
Of course.

29
00:02:47,693 --> 00:02:48,523
Right, Agumon?

30
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,777
Listen, buddy, this is your big chance.

31
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:51,690
Don't let me down.

32
00:02:51,773 --> 00:02:53,797
You're the only one that
can digivolve further,

33
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,817
so either you try to get to the
next level and save us from Etemon,

34
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,237
or I'll go and get myself a new Digimon.

35
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,660
Not much of a choice.

36
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:02,290
Arrgh!

37
00:03:02,373 --> 00:03:05,077
By the way, how are we supposed to
use the Crest to digivolve again?

38
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,937
Well, from what we've seen so
far with the other Digivolutions,

39
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:09,197
it takes a lot of energy.

40
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:11,857
For example, they can't
digivolve if they're hungry.

41
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:15,737
In addition, the partner of the
Digimon must be in some sort of danger.

42
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,257
You know, like being
under attack or something.

43
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:20,497
But since it's a higher
level of digivolving,

44
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,517
my theory is even more energy is needed.

45
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:26,012
So we'll provide the food,
Etemon will provide the danger.

46
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:35,197
You better watch out,
you Digidestined kids.

47
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,110
I'll find you.

48
00:03:36,193 --> 00:03:38,537
And when I do, you'll wish
you'll never cross, Etemon.

49
00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:39,450
I'll get you.

50
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,250
Hey, no more.

51
00:03:41,333 --> 00:03:43,320
Just one more teensy bite.

52
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,807
Ready for the second course?

53
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:48,617
Oh, stop your belly aching and open wide.

54
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,257
You've got to keep on eating.

55
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:53,237
Listen, everyone's given you their
food so that you can digivolve.

56
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,720
Isn't that right? Yeah.

57
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,957
We didn't give him our food.

58
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:58,077
He took it from us of all the nerve.

59
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,837
Well, the food won't do us any good.

60
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,277
We still can't digivolve.

61
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,337
So those of us who don't
work don't eat, huh?

62
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:04,340
But I'm hungry.

63
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,120
Hey, I can't hear you.

64
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,520
I said, is that right? That's right.

65
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:12,657
See, that's why you've got to try
your best to protect everybody.

66
00:04:12,740 --> 00:04:14,777
Now, come on, buddy. Keep eating.

67
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:17,684
I guess there's not much
else we can do to help.

68
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:20,197
I don't know if Agumon can take much more.

69
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,104
Yeah, Tai is really pushing him.

70
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:24,637
Agumon's stuffed like
a Thanksgiving turkey.

71
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,550
Eat up.

72
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:26,537
You need that energy.

73
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:29,177
Ty's personality has taken
a turn for the worse lately.

74
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,257
I remember him being friendlier
even to us younger kids.

75
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:36,222
Actually, now that you mention it,
he was cool during soccer camp.

76
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:38,719
Tai, pass it to me.

77
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:39,670
I'm open.

78
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,540
Now's my chance to shoot. Here I go.

79
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:58,597
Nice pass, Tai I thought you were going
to take the shot yourself Remember,

80
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:04,617
there's no I in team Tai might look
like he's trying to run things all by

81
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:09,288
himself But whatever crazy action he
takes He does it for the good of the team

82
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,260
But now all this

83
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:16,497
We're the only ones who can help now So
you've got to keep eating, okay, Agumon?

84
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,640
I can't.

85
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,657
Ty's personality seems
to have changed ever

86
00:05:20,740 --> 00:05:23,137
since he got a hold of
that crest of courage.

87
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,161
Boy, I'm hungry.

88
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,600
Hey, guys.

89
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,640
My tag is blowing.

90
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,801
It must be reacting to something.

91
00:05:31,260 --> 00:05:34,540
The crest must be near
a lie. You think so?

92
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,220
Hey, look.

93
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,337
There's something out there.

94
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:41,380
It looks like a big building or something.

95
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,904
That must be where my crest is.

96
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:51,161
What's a cable doing out
in the middle of nowhere?

97
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,300
What is it, Lord Entelon?

98
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:01,141
Something's caught in my network.

99
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,560
The intruder's in the L7 sector.

100
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,580
Let's see, L7, L7.

101
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:07,757
How's this thing work?

102
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,740
Oh, here it is.

103
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:10,420
Where is it?

104
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,417
It's near the Coliseum.

105
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:14,877
That's where I hold my
annual Tribute to Me show.

106
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,777
I wonder what they're doing
all the way over there.

107
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:17,860
You got any idea?

108
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:20,097
Well, maybe they want
to get good seats, boss.

109
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:23,297
Oh, we'll have a perfect view for the
surprise show I'm planning for them.

110
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:24,262
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

111
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,997
Hello, Area L7.

112
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:34,080
Can I help you? It's Etemon. Yes, sir.

113
00:06:34,660 --> 00:06:37,337
Hey, little bunny, you should
be having some guests soon.

114
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,157
You better get ready to welcome them.

115
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,070
Welcome them?

116
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,240
So do you mean... Bingo, bunny.

117
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,760
As you wish, sir.

118
00:07:10,380 --> 00:07:11,210
Amazing.

119
00:07:11,293 --> 00:07:13,000
It looks like the Roman Colosseum.

120
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,740
What's the Roman Colosseum?

121
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,162
Well, Tentomon,

122
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:21,125
it's an ancient arena But the ancient one
didn't have big screens Or soccer goals

123
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:32,678
Okay, guys, let's all split
up and look for the crest

124
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,030
What's wrong?

125
00:07:34,113 --> 00:07:38,500
I can't move anymore Let me rest
for a little bit Come on, get up,

126
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:43,700
you can do it I can't Give him a rest,
Tai The only clue we have is my tag.

127
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,057
So Gomamon and I will
search for the crest.

128
00:07:46,140 --> 00:07:47,297
You guys relax for a while.

129
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,733
Wait, I'll go with you.

130
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,840
A soccer ball.

131
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,560
Hey, anybody up for a game?

132
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,997
Yeah, that sounds fun.

133
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,137
That's a great idea.

134
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,497
The human team will play
against the Digimon team.

135
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,040
What on earth is soccer?

136
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:01,690
It's easy.

137
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,557
You use your feet to try to
get this ball into the goal.

138
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:07,052
You can also use your chest or your head.

139
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:10,140
Here I go.

140
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,280
Oh, that's really using your head.

141
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:16,837
Oh, and I forgot to tell you,
you can't use your hands.

142
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:20,057
Unless you're the goalkeeper, then you
can touch the ball with your hands.

143
00:08:20,140 --> 00:08:23,217
Yeah, you should be the
goalie for your team, Palmon.

144
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:24,130
Yeah!

145
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:28,810
What?

146
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,270
Oh!

147
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:33,290
Huh?

148
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:36,397
I can't believe you're playing
soccer at a time like this.

149
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,697
Will you use your heads for something
other than hitting the ball?

150
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:41,937
The sooner Joe finds the
crest, the sooner we can leave.

151
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:44,560
Your tag is reacting again. Yeah.

152
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,880
The crest must be around
here somewhere. Huh?

153
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:53,280
Who's the king?

154
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:54,920
Oh, he's here.

155
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:56,020
Agumon's here.

156
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,760
Wait for me.

157
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:01,930
Agumon.

158
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,980
We're trapped.

159
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,560
Goal. Gold!

160
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:08,937
I sure did it!

161
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:09,961
I scored a gold!

162
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,437
The whole thing was a trap!

163
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:14,696
Does he really think he can
trap us with a simple net?

164
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:17,740
Now, now, listen up.

165
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,597
If you do that, you might get hurt.

166
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:22,197
You see, there's electricity
running through that net.

167
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,633
It's a shocker, I know.

168
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:28,277
I really wanted to be there in person
to do this myself, but I'm way too busy.

169
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,417
You know how us rock and roll legends are.

170
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,657
But don't worry, the axe substituting
for me is a very rare treat.

171
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,570
Well,

172
00:09:34,653 --> 00:09:35,577
let's see if you can put
your puny little heads

173
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:39,280
together and figure out who our
special guest star is. Well?

174
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:41,247
How would we know who it is?

175
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,066
I'm sure you'll be surprised.

176
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,780
Here he comes.

177
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,211
It's a different Greymon.

178
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,740
Hey, I knew you'd be surprised.

179
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,460
I'm so evil.

180
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,400
Let's get started.

181
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:56,430
It's time to go.

182
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:57,794
Okay, here's the show.

183
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:05,680
It's time to Digivolve.

184
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:16,400
Digimon, Digimon, Digimon.

185
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:20,380
Digimon, Digimon.

186
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,240
Agumon!

187
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,500
Digiball, no!

188
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,800
Raymon!

189
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:39,780
Digimon!

190
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:49,037
You can do it, Koromon!

191
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:51,100
Don't lose to that bony baloney!

192
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:04,820
Koromon, you've got to digivolve!

193
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,020
Boy, this doesn't look good.

194
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:09,888
We're done for if you
can't digivolve again.

195
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:37,040
Digivolve, Koromon, you've got to!

196
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,577
What's he waiting for?

197
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,457
Why won't he digivolve to the next level?

198
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:53,597
It's not working, Tai.

199
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:55,217
The crust isn't reacting at all.

200
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,897
Maybe you gave him too much to eat.

201
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:58,451
Maybe he can't digivolve.

202
00:11:58,860 --> 00:11:59,860
Of course he can.

203
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,280
Come on, Greymon, you can do it.

204
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:05,048
Believe in your power
and you can digivolve.

205
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:08,960
Way to go, Greymon.

206
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,250
Nova Blast.

207
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:14,957
He certainly doesn't
have any digi manners.

208
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,137
At least they excuse me.

209
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:19,297
Am I imagining it, or is he
moving a lot slower than usual?

210
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:22,177
He consumed way too much, so
his reflexes are sluggish.

211
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,378
You're right, Izzy.

212
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:24,880
Not again.

213
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:28,700
Get up and fight!

214
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:39,204
It's looking like this is going
to be over sooner than I thought.

215
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:44,117
You silly rabbits stop carrying
on like a trained seal.

216
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:48,400
Get the fireworks ready so I can
celebrate my victory. Yes, sir!

217
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:56,000
We really need help!

218
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:57,140
Launching fishes!

219
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:10,517
Where did those fish come from?

220
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:13,037
How could they just come
out of there like that?

221
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,957
I don't know, but if it's
not broken, don't fix it.

222
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,357
It's really elementary, Joe.

223
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:20,177
There's probably just a dimensional
vortex rift in the water.

224
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,090
Ditto!

225
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:27,140
Thank you, fish!

226
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:30,817
Now, what are we going
to do to get out of here?

227
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:33,317
We should dig a hole
and tunnel our way out.

228
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:34,230
Good idea.

229
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,537
There's a black cable here, too.

230
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,032
This rock is in the way.

231
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:44,477
my tag it's it's reacting again what if

232
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:47,207
this rock is the crest
we've been looking for

233
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:58,480
if this really is the crest
that goes with my tag then maybe

234
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:18,460
it is my crest yes look a tunnel
we can get out through here

235
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:25,677
how do you like that not only
did those little darlings

236
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:29,289
escape but they found another
crest too this is unforgivable

237
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,725
Koromon, you could win
if you'd only Digivolve!

238
00:14:38,180 --> 00:14:39,010
Koromon!

239
00:14:39,860 --> 00:14:40,780
Tai, don't!

240
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:41,757
Don't stop me!

241
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,657
This is my chance to make him
Digivolve to the next level!

242
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:46,837
Please mind your own business, Sora!

243
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:51,277
But, Tai, without a reaction from the
crest, there's no way for him to Digivolve!

244
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:53,660
I can make him do it! Watch!

245
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:57,817
What do you think he's gonna do?

246
00:14:57,900 --> 00:15:02,076
The other condition for digivolving
is their partner must be in danger.

247
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,840
He wouldn't.

248
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,200
Hurry up and finish him off.

249
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,140
Use your Nova Blast.

250
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,440
I'm not afraid of a big fake like you.

251
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,899
Okay, fire breath.

252
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,360
Come and get me.

253
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,140
What do we have here?

254
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,897
A dope who thinks he's a superstar?

255
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:23,810
